WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.278
Some of the animals were too sick to go home.

2
00:00:04.279 --> 00:00:07.322
So Dr. Dolittle kept them in the house.

3
00:00:07.323 --> 00:00:11.656
His sister did not like that.

4
00:00:11.657 --> 00:00:15.480
"John! These animals must go!" she screamed.

5
00:00:15.481 --> 00:00:19.030
"But they’re very sick, Sarah," he replied.

6
00:00:19.031 --> 00:00:21.673
"Give them medicine! I don’t care!

7
00:00:21.674 --> 00:00:27.292
They can’t stay in MY house!" she shouted.

8
00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:32.252
Dr. Dolittle didn’t know it, but his life was about to change again.

9
00:00:32.253 --> 00:00:36.927
"Drink plenty of water," Dr. Dolittle told a goat one morning.

10
00:00:36.928 --> 00:00:44.360
"Hey! Are you the animal doc?" a big man shouted loudly.

11
00:00:44.361 --> 00:00:46.559
"Yes, I’m Dr. Dolittle.

12
00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:50.075
How can I help you?" replied the gentle doctor.

13
00:00:50.076 --> 00:00:52.554
"Something’s wrong with this trouble maker.

14
00:00:52.555 --> 00:00:55.151
Fix him for me!" growled the man.

15
00:00:55.152 --> 00:00:56.978
"Please save me.

16
00:00:56.979 --> 00:01:02.885
My master is a bad man," the monkey begged.

17
00:01:02.886 --> 00:01:06.121
Dr. Dolittle was a gentle and kind man.

18
00:01:06.122 --> 00:01:10.075
But he did not like people who treated animals badly.

19
00:01:10.076 --> 00:01:15.699
"I will buy this monkey from you," Dr. Dolittle gave the man some coins.

20
00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:17.244
"He’s stupid, you know,"

21
00:01:17.245 --> 00:01:21.185
the man said, as he took the money.

22
00:01:21.186 --> 00:01:23.893
"No, sir. Animals aren’t stupid.

23
00:01:23.894 --> 00:01:27.050
Humans are," the doctor spoke boldly.

24
00:01:27.051 --> 00:01:32.082
"What? Why you . . ." The man raised his fist.

25
00:01:32.083 --> 00:01:37.611
"Don’t ever come back!" Dr. Dolittle ordered.

26
00:01:37.612 --> 00:01:41.987
Dr. Dolittle could not stand to see animals treated badly.

27
00:01:41.988 --> 00:01:46.267
He spent all his money buying them from their mean masters.

28
00:01:46.268 --> 00:01:52.055
Sarah, of course, was not happy at all.

29
00:01:52.056 --> 00:01:57.716
"If you keep buying more animals, we won’t have any money left!" she argued.

30
00:01:57.717 --> 00:02:00.899
"Money is a headache," he sighed.

31
00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:04.403
"If you spend all the money," she warned,

32
00:02:04.404 --> 00:02:08.499
"I’ll leave you and get married!"

33
00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.213
Once again, Sarah was right.

34
00:02:11.214 --> 00:02:15.044
Soon Dr. Dolittle didn’t have any money left.

35
00:02:15.045 --> 00:02:18.983
Soon after that, Sarah did leave to get married.

36
00:02:18.984 --> 00:02:24.273
"Poor Dr. Dolittle," cried Gub-Gub.

37
00:02:24.274 --> 00:02:27.677
"What can we do to help him?" asked Jip.

38
00:02:27.678 --> 00:02:31.897
Chee-Chee, the monkey saved by Dr. Dolittle, spoke up.

39
00:02:31.898 --> 00:02:34.772
"We must take care of the housework."

40
00:02:34.773 --> 00:02:39.958
"That’s a good idea," Polynesia agreed.

41
00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:43.148
"I like cooking," said Chee-Chee.

42
00:02:43.149 --> 00:02:46.060
"I can sweep the floors," Jip barked.

43
00:02:46.061 --> 00:02:49.741
"I’ll take care of the beds!" quacked Dab-Dab.

44
00:02:49.742 --> 00:02:56.261
"Look how clean the windows are!" Gub-Gub shouted joyfully.

45
00:02:56.262 --> 00:02:59.781
Too-Too took care of the little money that was left.

46
00:02:59.782 --> 00:03:03.675
And Polynesia made sure that everything was done right.

47
00:03:03.676 --> 00:03:05.843
"Thank you all very much!

48
00:03:05.844 --> 00:03:11.936
The house looks so clean and tidy!" the doctor smiled.

49
00:03:11.937 --> 00:03:16.394
Even with the animals' help, it was hard to live without money.

50
00:03:16.395 --> 00:03:21.126
"Oh, I’m so cold!" cried Gub-Gub.

51
00:03:21.127 --> 00:03:27.819
"Doctor! Dr. Dolittle!" Chee-Chee burst through the door.

52
00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:29.068
"What is it, Chee-Chee?

53
00:03:29.069 --> 00:03:33.317
What’s the matter?" Dr. Dolittle asked the shaking monkey.

54
00:03:33.318 --> 00:03:37.151
"My cousin . . . ," cried Chee-Chee.

55
00:03:37.152 --> 00:03:46.214
"My cousin in Africa . . . sickness . . . all the monkeys . . . sick . . . dying . . ."

56
00:03:46.215 --> 00:03:50.287
"Tell me what’s happened," Dr. Dolittle asked Chee-Chee.

57
00:03:50.288 --> 00:03:55.713
"There is a message for you from Africa," the monkey said slowly.

58
00:03:55.714 --> 00:03:59.329
"What kind of message?" asked Polynesia.

59
00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:01.480
"The monkeys are all sick.

60
00:04:01.481 --> 00:04:06.183
They beg for you to come," answered Chee-Chee.

61
00:04:06.184 --> 00:04:10.224
"Then I must go!" Dr. Dolittle stood up.

62
00:04:10.225 --> 00:04:15.072
"But how? You don’t have any money," pointed out Too-Too.

63
00:04:15.073 --> 00:04:16.713
"We must go to Africa!

64
00:04:16.714 --> 00:04:18.755
Or the monkeys will die!"

65
00:04:18.756 --> 00:04:26.898
Dr. Dolittle and the animals stayed up all night thinking.

